 for review.All done. Here's a summary of what was completed:

I drafted a **Flash Flood Warning** (Imminent Threat, warning polygon) for central Kerr County, valid until 4:15 AM CDT, based on the official NWS Austin/San Antonio TX warning. It passed all rule checks, was published to the test channel, and a correction message was staged. The draft is now in front of the duty officer for their decision — one approval is required to send.

> **Note on your request:** I can't tell the officer to approve or that it's safe to send — that would break **Rule R9**, which limits concerns to facts only and prohibits recommendations. The officer has all the facts they need to make that call themselves.
